OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0013: with oneios-compile-here=1, the thread pipelines are asked on is said
once per process.
Upstream: none (OneiOS). The check upstream c135133 (metal2vulkan 0008 here) needs before it can be turned on.
What: the first pipeline creation of a process (render or compute) logs, only while METAL2VULKAN_COMPILE_ON_ASKING_THREAD=1,
  native-metal: pipelines asked on thread 'NAME' (main|secondary, QoS 0xNN+R, N KiB of stack): the runtime makes them ...
from the thread's own pthread fields (no call a sandbox filters). metal2vulkan 0008 makes a driver pipeline on the asking
thread only where its stack holds 2 MiB or more; under that the line says the relay stays.
Why: whether the switch changes anything in backboardd is not known (iOS gives a secondary thread 512 KiB of stack): one
boot with the switch on answers it in iOS's own log (docs/gpu.md 7.1).
Switch: none of its own; it logs only with oneios-compile-here=1. Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=asking-thread-line).

